From: ZenTao Runtime <runtime@zentao.net>
Subject: [PATCH] Zend: export disabled signal ABI required by ionCube

FrankenPHP disables Zend signal handling to avoid conflicting with the Go
runtime. ionCube Loader 15.5 for PHP 8.4 TS still resolves three signal ABI
symbols. Export inert values without enabling Zend signal handling.

The globals remain zero-initialized. ionCube checks zend_signal_globals_id
before using the TSRM offset, so its signal interruption path stays disabled.
---
 Zend/zend_signal.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Zend/zend_signal.c b/Zend/zend_signal.c
index 8b4b8b0..cd04b79 100644
--- a/Zend/zend_signal.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_signal.c
@@ -446,3 +446,13 @@ ZEND_API void zend_signal_check(void)
 
 
 #endif /* ZEND_SIGNALS */
+
+#if !defined(ZEND_SIGNALS) && defined(ZTS)
+/*
+ * ionCube Loader 15.5 resolves these symbols even when Zend Signals are
+ * disabled. Keep the globals zero so the loader never enters that path.
+ */
+ZEND_API int zend_signal_globals_id;
+ZEND_API size_t zend_signal_globals_offset;
+ZEND_API void zend_signal_handler_unblock(void) {}
+#endif
